      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2012 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A novel 4-aminocyclopentapyrrolidine series of N-type Ca(2+) channel blockers have been discovered. Enantioselective synthesis of the 4-aminocyclopentapyrrolidines was enabled using N-tert-butyl sulfinamide chemistry. SAR studies demonstrate selectivity over L-type Ca(2+) channels. N-type Ca(2+) channel blockade was confirmed using electrophysiological recording techniques. Compound 25 is an N-type Ca(2+) channel blocker that produces antinociception in inflammatory and nociceptive pain models without exhibiting cardiovascular or motor liabilities."
      },
